<title>GERMANY: ProSieben boosts sales, profit in Q1.</title>
<headline>ProSieben boosts sales, profit in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>UNTERFOEHRING, Germany 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>First quarter</p>
<p>1997. (in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		    84	 vs 63</p>
<p>    Group sales				479	 up 17.5 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Television station ProSieben Media AG is currently owned outright by Thomas Kirch and the Rewe retail group, but will be listed on the Frankfurt stock market in July.</p>
<p>The company said it expected significant increases in both sales and pre-tax profits this year. Last year turnover rose by 15 percent to 1.69 billion marks, while income on ordinary activities climbed by 59 percent to 178 million marks.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
